# PROSM Time - environment strategy (WP-01).
#
# Two distinct trust levels, never mixed:
#
# 1. VITE_-prefixed variables are bundled into the CLIENT build and are
#    PUBLIC by construction (anyone can read them from the shipped JS).
#    Only PROSM Time's OWN Supabase project's public URL/anon key belong
#    here - never a secret, never anything from PROSM Management.
#
# 2. Everything below the line is a SERVER-SIDE secret, used only by
#    PROSM Time's own Supabase Edge Functions (via `supabase secrets
#    set`, never committed, never exposed to the browser). This is
#    where the PROSM Management integration API key lives - it
#    authenticates PROSM Time's OWN backend to PROSM Management's
#    integration contract (prosm-management-integration Edge Function)
#    and must never reach client code, per the Master File's own
#    "never share auth secrets between the two systems" (§6/§43.6).

# --- Client (VITE_-prefixed, public) ---
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Server-side only (Edge Function secrets, set via `supabase secrets set`) ---
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is provisioned automatically by Supabase for
# every Edge Function - never set manually, listed here only for
# documentation completeness.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# PROSM Management integration contract (§6/§35) - issued once from
# PROSM Management's Product Registry (Regenerate/Generate API key on
# the PROSM Time product row), shown only once at issuance.
PROSM_MANAGEMENT_API_URL=
PROSM_MANAGEMENT_API_KEY=
